rations and startup output contains an error.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API process starts.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is running and its configured database becomes unavailable during a contracted operation.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-18.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 500 with the contract-defined `server_error` code and no success response or success record is returned.\",\n     \"when\": \"The operation is called.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall fail startup when persistent-storage configuration is invalid and return the contract-defined server-error response without reporting a business operation as successful when storage is unavailable during a contracted operation.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-18\",\n   \"op\": \"ADDED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-2\",\n    \"I-3\",\n    \"Q-8\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"Every operation and response case defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, including contract-valid and contract-invalid requests and the declared authentication and authorization cases.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status, content type, response fields, and error body conform to that operation's OpenAPI request and response definitions.\",\n     \"when\": \"A test client sends the corresponding HTTP requests to every declared operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A caller authenticated as an account with assigned warehouse or organization scopes calls a collection or record operation using contract-defined filters.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status and returned list or record contain only data within the caller's assigned scope and reflect the supplied filters.\",\n     \"when\": \"The caller sends the HTTP request to that operation.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The API is running with valid startup configuration.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-19.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status for each request is 200.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client requests `GET /`, `GET /openapi/v1.json`, and `GET /swagger`.\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"anchors\": [\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 12,\n     \"lineStart\": 1,\n     \"path\": \"contracts/openapi.yaml\",\n     \"quote\": \"openapi: 3.0.3\\ninfo:\\n  title: Meridian Cold Chain API\\n  version: 1.0.0\\n  description: \\\"Shared contract for the Meridian responsive web portal.\\\"\\nservers:\\n  - url: /api\\npaths:\\n  /auth/staff/authorization-url:\\n    get:\\n      operationId: getStaffAuthorizationUrl\\n      summary: \\\"Get the configured staff identity-provider authorization URL.\\\"\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"lineEnd\": 31,\n     \"lineStart\": 28,\n     \"path\": \"App.Api/Program.cs\",\n     \"quote\": \"app.MapGet(\\\"/\\\", () => \\\"API is up\\\").ExcludeFromDescription();\\n// The API's own document (/openapi/v1.json) and a page to read and try it (/swagger). Keep both: the factory's product page links to the page.\\napp.MapOpenApi();\\napp.UseSwaggerUI(o => o.SwaggerEndpoint(\\\"/openapi/v1.json\\\", \\\"API\\\"));\"\n    }\n   ],\n   \"ears\": \"The Meridian API shall implement only the operations and behavior defined in `contracts/openapi.yaml`, with the existing root health, OpenAPI-document, and Swagger UI routes retained.\",\n   \"id\": \"REQ-19\",\n   \"op\": \"MODIFIED\",\n   \"sources\": [\n    \"I-1\",\n    \"I-5\",\n    \"Q-1\"\n   ],\n   \"stability\": 1\n  },\n  {\n   \"acceptance\": [\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database and a valid request to a contract operation that creates or changes persistent business data.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.1\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is the operation's contract-declared success status, the returned record identifier and values reflect the requested change, and the persisted row values match that change.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client calls the operation and then reads the affected entity through the corresponding contract operation or directly from the database.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A configured PostgreSQL database and a valid receipt input.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.2\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, the returned record status is Quarantined, and the persisted row status is Quarantined.\",\n     \"when\": \"A client calls `POST /api/warehouse/receipts` and reads the resulting receipt.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"A customer-owned order that is before packing and a valid order change input.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.3\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, and the returned record and persisted row reflect the change.\",\n     \"when\": \"The authenticated customer sends a valid `PATCH /api/customer/orders/{orderId}` request.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"An existing PostgreSQL database contains existing records and a reviewed migration introduces the required schema changes.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.4\",\n     \"level\": \"job\",\n     \"then\": \"The existing row values remain unchanged and the database table list contains the migrated schema.\",\n     \"when\": \"The deployment migration runs against that database.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The configured PostgreSQL database has no tables.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.5\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200 and the database table list contains the contract-backed tables.\",\n     \"when\": \"The API starts and a client requests `GET /`.\"\n    },\n    {\n     \"given\": \"The configured PostgreSQL database has at least one table and existing records, and a reviewed migration is pending.\",\n     \"id\": \"AC-20.6\",\n     \"level\": \"api\",\n     \"then\": \"The response status is 200, existing row values remain unchanged, and the database table list matches its pre